From 9303e5d368d9c809830b33cf11b634b9cdb05e3f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qizixi <22851944+zixi-qi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:59:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 26/53] [Spec Decode][MRV2] Warm up top-k/top-p and greedy
 rejection kernels for speculative decoding (#59260)

Upstream c1407a7e86a8666cb9223e8e2b818ef4b81e53c0 (merged 2026-10-14), with
its upstream follow-up folded in:

  [Bugfix][MRV2] Fix speculative warmup deadlock with pipeline parallelism
  (#62129, 7c9042c05addf034366b9a1da5b1d3e3687c052b): the greedy round is
  keyed on speculative_config, not rejection_sampler, so every PP rank runs
  the same warmup forwards.

#62129 brings test_kernel_warmup_runs_same_rounds_on_every_pp_stage, which
the #63819 / #63421 picks on this branch had dropped; it is restored here in
upstream main's form (speculator=None from #63819).

B70-V6x: the greedy warmup round is opt-in, B70_SPEC_GREEDY_WARMUP=1
(default off), so startup with the flag unset runs the same rounds as
before. The env is process-wide, so all PP ranks take the same branch. The
restored PP test is parametrized over the flag. The model_runner.py hunk
(top-k/top-p warmups on CUDA with a speculative config) is unchanged from
upstream and does not run on XPU.

Supersedes riceharvest f829c492aa patch_spec_greedy_warmup (same backport,
commit 2 only).

Signed-off-by: zixi-qi <zixi@inferact.ai>
Signed-off-by: chenjr97 <chenjr97@mail2.sysu.edu.cn>
Co-authored-by: Junru Chen <114817987+chenjr97@users.noreply.github.com>
Co-authored-by: Nick Hill <nickhill123@gmail.com>
Co-authored-by: vllm-agent <claw@inferact.ai>
Co-authored-by: mergify[bot] <37929162+mergify[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
